            <title>[LU-21133] TCU: ltrash_purge cannot reclaim Trash Can entries when the MDT keeps the original ownership with audit disabled</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21133</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Problem&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;With &lt;tt&gt;trash_can_{uid,gid,projid}=original&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;trash_can_audit=0&lt;/tt&gt;, the MDT writes no &lt;tt&gt;trusted.unrm&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;ltrash_purge&lt;/tt&gt; then drops every entry ("Cannot read unrm xattr"), so &lt;tt&gt;-&lt;del&gt;max-age&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;&lt;del&gt;uid&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;&lt;del&gt;gid&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;-projid&lt;/tt&gt; never purge anything; &lt;tt&gt;lfs trash state -p&lt;/tt&gt; reports projid 0.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In the same configuration the daemon never scans at all: &lt;tt&gt;ltrash_purge_trash_is_empty()&lt;/tt&gt; reports "empty" when the trash project ID is &lt;tt&gt;original&lt;/tt&gt;, cannot be read, or the quota call fails unexpectedly ("Trash Can is empty, skip scan.").&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;With only an age or ID policy (no watermark), a scan reuses the MDT/OST usage sampled by a previous scan, and the "check every N deletions" logic stops the scan after the first N deletions even though the policy still matches.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Threshold handling was inconsistent: the per-entry check used &lt;tt&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt; while the scan trigger used &lt;tt&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/tt&gt;, so entries were not purged exactly at the watermark.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Impact&lt;/b&gt; Trash Can space is never reclaimed for the "original UGP + no audit" configuration (the documented way to keep per-user quota accounting), the daemon can sleep indefinitely, and watermark purging differs from what &lt;tt&gt;ltrash_purge.8&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;ltrash_purge.conf&lt;/tt&gt; describe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Expected&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Missing &lt;tt&gt;trusted.unrm&lt;/tt&gt;: age/UID/GID filters keep working from the object's own attributes, project ID read with &lt;tt&gt;FS_IOC_FSGETXATTR&lt;/tt&gt;, project-ID filter skipped when it cannot be read (e.g. symlink); &lt;tt&gt;lfs trash state -p&lt;/tt&gt; reports the real project ID.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Scan is skipped only when the usage is actually known to be zero.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Each scan samples the MDT/OST usage; a scan stops only when no policy matches.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/tt&gt; everywhere; documentation states that policies are combined with OR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
